      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit:\n\nthe order of loading in RevCommitCG was:\n\n1. if isRetainBody, fill buffer via cached byte, aka getCachedBytes, then read the rest from graph or buffer. if !isRetainBody, read from graph directly.\n2. marked as PARSED.\n\nThe reason this isRetainBody-first decision making works for RevCommitCG is because RevCommitCG is only introduced by CG object so it\u0027s implied that it has a position in the CG.\n\nthe order of loading in RevCommit of this change is:\n\n1. read header specific data from CG if the position \u003e 0.\n2. handle the retainBody logic and getCachedByte within the parseInGraph or parseCanonical methods independently. \n3. marked as PARSED.\n\nI believe the IO cost is the same comparing the pre-regression code path and the code change in this change, but it\u0027s worth disclosing.",
